WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.270
- She's an inspiration to Alicia, myself,

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:05.170
and millions of women worldwide.

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:08.300
She's an author, an activist,
her latest book "Untamed"

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.490
was released in March and has already sold

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:11.690
over 1 million copies.

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:12.900
I am two of those.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.782
Please welcome Glennon Doyle, everybody!

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:19.230
(audience applauding)

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:20.410
Okay, so first of all.

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:21.460
- Hi Kelly!

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:22.920
- I love that you two actually

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.140
already know each other, right?

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:26.050
- We're connected.
- We do.

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:28.990
Well I have, yes, deeply connected.

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:30.380
I have actually been deeply connected

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:32.580
to Alicia for decades,
but she just found out

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:34.021
about it a couple years ago.

00:00:34.021 --> 00:00:35.163
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:35.163 --> 00:00:37.490
We just started the two-way
friendship recently.

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:39.350
It's just been me singing her songs

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:42.670
and crying in the shower for
many, many years until now.

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:44.330
- That's all of us.

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.490
But Glennon, so many
people have read "Untamed",

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:48.340
especially people that I know.

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:50.520
And they've found inspiration.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:53.390
But for people not
familiar, what is it about?

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:55.680
What would you say if you
had to give a synopsis?

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.240
- Well the storyline,
the main storyline going

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:01.110
through it, is I was in a
broken marriage to a good man,

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:02.510
and that is a hard place for a woman

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:04.640
to be because we're
supposed to be grateful

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:06.430
for what we have and
good enough is supposed

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:07.330
to be good enough.

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:12.421
But as that marriage,
as we were struggling

00:01:12.421 --> 00:01:15.740
to kind find some
unbrokenness, I fell madly

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:16.793
in love with a woman.

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:20.820
And I don't know, when I met her this part

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:24.180
of me rose up that I had
abandoned a long time ago,

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:26.390
and I just was faced with this kind

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:28.250
of life-or-death situation it felt like.

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:30.730
Like, am I going to abandon the self

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:33.810
because I'm too afraid to
rock the boat of my life?

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:34.740
- Mm-hm.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:39.040
- Or am I going to abandon
everyone else's expectations

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:41.953
of me and honor myself for
the first time in my life?

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:44.820
- Alicia's freakin' out right now!

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:46.347
I don't know if you
can see her (laughing).

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:48.930
And you did, you did.

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:50.160
- [Glennon] I did honor myself.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:53.614
- You did "Me X 7", that's one
of her new songs. (laughing)

00:01:53.614 --> 00:01:55.610
(Alicia squealing and laughing)

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:57.570
- [Glennon] Yes I did.

00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:00.260
When we do finally honor ourselves,

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:02.140
we have been trained to believe that

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:04.200
that will somehow hurt our people,

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.320
and sometimes it makes them
uncomfortable at first.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:08.160
But what happens when we honor ourselves

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:11.020
is we give permission to
everyone else in our families

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:13.300
and our lives to honor themselves also.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.730
So it's a freedom that is contagious.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:18.100
- Yeah, what a great domino effect, yes.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:20.120
So Glennon we have an important election

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:21.167
in less than three weeks, and Alicia

00:02:21.167 --> 00:02:22.640
and I were talking a little bit

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:24.800
about, you know just what's happening

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:26.470
in the world right now.

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:30.000
I will say, I have totally
stalked you online,

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.820
I've seen everything and I
know all your story. (laughing)

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:36.390
But one thing I love that you talk about,

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:37.640
and I think it was actually a couple years

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:38.830
ago maybe even that you
first started talking

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:40.847
about, but people were like, "Oh my gosh,

00:02:40.847 --> 00:02:43.360
2020's gonna be the death,
everything is horrible,

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:45.190
it's the apocalypse."

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:47.960
And I loved that it takes
sometimes that deconstruction,

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:51.300
that blowing up of
things, to actually sort

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:54.660
out all the crap that's actually wrong.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:56.500
Are you hopeful or are you still kind

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:59.440
of like, "Oh my gosh,
like what's happening?"

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:02.380
- Two things, I mean I
use the word apocalypse.

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:04.480
Apocalypse means uncovering.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:05.313
- Yep.
- Right?

00:03:05.313 --> 00:03:08.010
So in terms of what this time is doing,

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:09.960
none of this that's happening, none

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:12.500
of this injustice and
inequality is new at all, right?

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:15.347
Which is why my activist
friends aren't the ones saying,

00:03:15.347 --> 00:03:17.770
"Oh my God, 2020 is the worst!"

00:03:17.770 --> 00:03:19.800
They're actually feeling
hopeful because this is,

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:21.480
all of this inequality has been going on

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:22.330
for a very long time.

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:25.080
It's just that now people
are finally seeing it because

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:28.460
of the apocalypse, uncovering of COVID.

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:29.840
As to whether I'm hopeful or not,

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:31.990
I heard Stacey Abrams say the other day.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:33.230
Someone said, "Are you hopeful?"

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:35.890
And she said, "I am neither
hopeful nor pessimistic,

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:37.430
I am determined."

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:38.263
- Ooh!

00:03:38.263 --> 00:03:40.530
- And I loved that so much because

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:44.440
as someone who's sober, I
rely on what I can control.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:46.820
And I know what I can't
control is outcome,

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:49.920
so pessimism and optimism
are reliant on outcome.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:53.510
But determinism, being
determined, that all has

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:56.780
to do with our input, how
we're showing up, right?

00:03:56.780 --> 00:04:00.840
So what I know is I am
determined over the next weeks

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.800
to get every single untamed woman I know

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:06.740
to refuse being gaslit,
to know what she knows,

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:10.290
feel what she feels, and
to show up at the polls

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:11.296
on November 3rd.

00:04:11.296 --> 00:04:12.229
(audience applauding)

00:04:12.229 --> 00:04:13.062
- Amen!

00:04:13.062 --> 00:04:15.170
Alicia, how are you
feeling about everything?

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:16.720
Like the voting and everything?

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:18.640
I know that everybody
always gets frustrated

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:20.980
with people in the music
world and art world

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:22.650
and they're like, "Just be artistic!"

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:25.100
And I'm like yes, but also
like I'm not pushing my views

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:27.280
on you but you have to realize how I think

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:29.460
because we've traveled,
we see how lucky we are,

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:31.930
how fortunate we are to be able to vote.

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:33.100
I don't know, I feel like it's kind

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:34.890
of your duty as an American citizen

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:36.980
to say something like that, you know?

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:39.690
- I mean it is, it is all
of our responsibility.

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:44.690
It's all of our opportunity
and definitely it is,

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:48.560
it's something that we should
all feel really actually

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:53.390
excited and passionate about, you know?

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:55.320
We can all learn so much more.

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:57.450
I think that's one thing
that I think about a lot.

00:04:57.450 --> 00:04:58.760
You don't have to know it all.

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:00.830
I think that's one of the
things that feels intimidating,

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:03.710
you're like, "Whoa, I'm not
sure" and how about this?

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:05.690
And it's okay that you don't know it all.

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:08.240
And it's okay to actually
start to learn more.

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:10.630
I think that's something
that I'm asking my friends

00:05:10.630 --> 00:05:14.330
and family and also just
anybody who's connecting

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:16.610
with me, like let's take a moment

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:18.780
to actually dig into
the parts we don't know.

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:20.410
Let's dig into the parts of the ballot

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:22.160
that maybe we are a
little bit insecure about

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:25.170
or the names that we're
not so clear about,

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:27.710
or the policies that maybe
don't make perfect sense,

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:30.720
or that we didn't take the
time to look into enough yet.

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:32.960
It's okay, it's all a growing process

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:36.860
and it's all a part of
actively being a human being.

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:38.360
You know, and actively being able

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:42.740
to be a participant in what
this whole thing looks like.

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:43.940
I mean, this is up to us.

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:46.600
This is not something where
it's like, "Oh we're gonna hope

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:50.950
that that one guy or
woman does the thing."

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:51.930
No!

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:55.640
One person can't do
anything all by themselves.

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:57.380
We all need to show up.

00:05:57.380 --> 00:06:00.340
We have to show up for our
families, for our own kids,

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:02.770
for our sisters and brothers,
for our communities.

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:04.630
Because if we're not showing
up, no one else is gonna be

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.480
like, "Oh hey, what's
happening in your spot?

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:08.070
'Cause I care so much about you."

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:11.180
No, we have to care about ourselves.

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:12.013
- Yeah.

00:06:12.013 --> 00:06:14.880
- We have to care about
ourselves enough to show up.

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:18.300
So it's less about that they're
gonna do all this stuff,

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.720
and we gotta show up for us, you know?

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:22.350
Less about them, more about us.

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:25.680
And let's learn about what
we can so that we can align

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:27.680
with people that have
similar beliefs and thoughts.

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:28.513
(audience applauding)

00:06:28.513 --> 00:06:31.630
But man, this is for us, we gotta do this.

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:33.040
- Thank you so much, Glennon.

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:34.920
And thank you Alicia, thank you

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:36.609
for being open and honest.

00:06:36.609 --> 00:06:37.442
(audience clapping)

00:06:37.442 --> 00:06:39.350
That kind of rawness is so rare

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:40.820
in this world in the public eye.

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:43.290
So I really appreciate
it and I'm lifting both

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:46.780
of you up and everybody pick
up "Untamed" by Glennon Doyle.

00:06:46.780 --> 00:06:49.520
I absolutely love this book
and it's available everywhere.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:51.340
Also pick up "Alicia"!

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:53.340
Her new album "Alicia" is out right now!

